    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule in `ClinicServiceImpl.toBusinessDay(...)` to also skip public holidays.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`):\n- Added a `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` constant set with the five fixed dates: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Replaced the old weekend-only `switch` (which handled just Saturday/Sunday in a single jump) with a loop that rolls the date forward one day at a time while it's a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a listed holiday. The loop correctly handles chains \u2014 e.g. a holiday that then lands on a weekend, or consecutive holidays \u2014 rolling forward to the next genuine business day.\n- Added the `java.time.DayOfWeek` import.\n\nThis mirrors the reference algorithm in the test base (`AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay`). `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests passing.",
